{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nSeventeen surviving Python modules under `tests/unit` contain 31 surviving audited prose blocks: 27 true leading docstrings and 4 full-line comment regions. Scope was revalidated against `origin/main@dac8df606ac5d4732a53cc02be976ee856ca209d`. Composite numeric spans around the compact sidecar block are collapsed to one real token region; executable tails are removed. The roster now calls `budget.pack_container_bins`, and a concise context-hint docstring still claims a removed orchestrator binding, so that stale block is explicitly added.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only the stable-ID blocks below. For every owned path, retain immutable before and final blobs and parse both with `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`. On comparison copies, remove only an allowlisted leading `Expr(Constant(str))` that is the first statement of a `Module`, `ClassDef`, `FunctionDef`, or `AsyncFunctionDef`; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; require the remaining normalized ASTs to match.\n\nTokenize both blobs and reject every changed inline comment or non-allowlisted full-line comment. Preserve non-docstring runtime strings, regexes, prompts, imports, decorators, annotations, assertions, subprocess arguments, test data, shebangs, and complete directive-bearing physical lines exactly. Adjacent blank-line normalization is allowed only around an edited block.\n\n## Stable block allowlist\n- `tests/unit/test_compact_trigger.py` — 4 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `D:_trigger_async_here`\n  - `D:test_the_close_neither_folds_nor_holds_the_lock`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def _canonical_store(tmp_path: Path) -> str:`\n- `tests/unit/test_completion_bank_observer_forwarding.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_completion_banking_oracle.py` — 4 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `D:test_intended_batched_shape_is_accepted`\n  - `D:test_fallback_only_transcript_is_bounded_and_green`\n  - `D:test_live_run_32575679530_shape_is_green_under_system_scope`\n- `tests/unit/test_completion_child_gate_scan_count.py` — 2 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `D:test_child_gate_scan_count_constant_in_child_count`\n- `tests/unit/test_completion_sidecar_lock_loss_ab54.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_completion_verifier_diag_e458.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline_lock_47e9.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py` — 2 blocks:\n  - `C:<module>:before:_KEY = \"src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py::close_ticket\"`\n  - `D:test_tree_assertions_agree_with_gate_on_a_reduction`\n- `tests/unit/test_config_gate_wiring_heldout.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_config_resolved_statuses_removal.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_config_show.py` — 2 blocks:\n  - `D:_clean_config_env`\n  - `D:test_module_fixtures_do_not_leak_real_user_config`\n- `tests/unit/test_config_writer_surface.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_conflict_bug_filing_js_safe_timestamps.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_container_roster.py` — 3 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `D:test_roster_builder_single_sourced`\n  - `D:test_roster_rides_prefix_not_instructions`\n- `tests/unit/test_container_warm_abort.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_context_hints_single_source.py` — 2 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `D:test_sizing_still_exposes_a_patchable_predicate`\n- `tests/unit/test_core_cli_parsers.py` — 3 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def store(tmp_path: Path, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch) -> Path:`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def _rejecting_parser(prog: str) -> RebarArgumentParser:`\n\n`D:<symbol>` is a true leading docstring. `C:<scope>:before:<code>` is one maximal full-line comment region anchored to unchanged code. No other prose is editable. In reviewer TSV, `stable_block_id` is the path-qualified `<path>#<D:...>` or `<path>#<C:...>` value.\n\n## Protected false positives\nAll unlisted prose and every executable/directive line are protected. In particular, the current concise `D:test_roster_counted_in_prefix_estimate` text names `budget.pack_container_bins` and stays exact; the added context-hint ID alone carries the stale removed-binding claim.\n\n## Preserved contracts and consumers\n- Compaction prose keeps operation-linked portability, async delegation, test isolation, lock/stamp/log ownership, symlink canonicalization, and structural no-inline-fold evidence.\n- Completion prose keeps response-denominated banking, actor-neutral durable writes, constant child scans, retry-and-loud-loss sidecars, signed diagnostics, and deterministic sampling.\n- Complexity/config prose keeps shrink-only merge-base comparison, local/CI parity, fail-closed locks, warn-class tombstones, late binding, hermetic config layers, and public writer identity.\n- Conflict/container/parser prose keeps JS-safe timestamps, AC-bearing cached rosters, warm abort/degrade classes, one context-hint definition with the current callable surface, and parser factories as the governing runtime grammar.\n- All modules are direct pytest inputs; `tests._bank_observer` is the shared dependency for the two banking suites. Mechanism baselines and sibling workflow/mechanism tests reference the named paths. No external target-module import, `__doc__`, `inspect.getdoc`, or pydoc consumer was found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Prose changes occur only inside the 31 declared stable-ID blocks.\n- [ ] Any changed blank line is adjacent to an edited stable-ID block.\n- [ ] The normalized-AST comparison passes on every owned path.\n- [ ] The token/comment comparison passes on every owned path.\n- [ ] A non-author reviewer posts exactly 31 leaf-linked TSV rows, one for each declared stable-ID block.\n- [ ] Every reviewer row uses this schema: stable_block_id<TAB>before_citation<TAB>final_citation<TAB>preserved_contract_or_consumer<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>before_words<TAB>after_words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer_session.\n- [ ] Every before_citation equals dac8df606ac5d4732a53cc02be976ee856ca209d:<path>#<stable-id>.\n- [ ] Every final_citation equals <final-commit-sha>:<path>#<stable-id>.\n- [ ] Every row records after_words < before_words.\n- [ ] Every row records directives_exact=PASS.\n- [ ] Every row records semantic-preservation=PASS, confirming its preserved_contract_or_consumer.\n- [ ] Every row records bloat-removal=PASS, confirming removal of chronology, duplication, obvious narration, or separator ornament.\n- [ ] All five structured verify commands pass.\n## Verification\nThe five DD-level commands recorded on this ticket run focused pytest (including real consumers), scoped Ruff check plus format-check, comment hygiene, owned-path `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify`. They are the executable completion oracle.\n\nCurrent main deleted `tests/unit/test_config_resolver_seam.py`; its 1 audited block is excluded from the surviving scope and independent review.\n\nCurrent-base correction: Group12's actual commit parent is `dac8df606ac5d4732a53cc02be976ee856ca209d`; 11 of the 33 combined paths changed after the earlier freeze. Review receipts cite this parent for before blocks and the final grouped commit for after blocks."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792761326829902957,"uuid":"648ef708-9576-4a1d-9227-3d2aee764890"}